meta {
  name: Reply To Note
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/notes
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "parentNoteId": {{noteId}},
    "content": "Bill uploaded, amount 4,200"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  bru.setEnvVar("replyNoteId", res.body.data.id);
}

docs {
  Replies to an existing note. Same endpoint as "Create Note", with `parentNoteId` in place of the
  entity: the reply takes its entity and torg from the note it answers. `entityType`/`entityId` may be
  sent too, but must then match the parent.

  Replies nest: reply to a reply by sending that reply's id as `parentNoteId`. In the response,
  `parentNoteId` is the note answered, `rootNoteId` is the top-level note of the thread and `depth` is
  how many levels down the reply sits. Safety limits: 100 levels deep and 500 replies per thread.

  Run "Create Note" first (it sets `noteId`). The reply's id is saved to `replyNoteId`.

  Returns the reply in `data`. 404 "Note not found" if the parent doesn't exist or belongs to another torg.
  400 "Cannot reply to a deleted note", if the entity sent doesn't match the parent's, or if the
  thread has hit a limit above.
}
